ORIGINAL WORK AND ATTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project began from "LLM Council" by Andrej Karpathy:

    https://github.com/karpathy/llm-council

That project introduced the multi-model deliberation approach on which the
general council mode is based — parallel model responses, anonymised peer
review with self-vote exclusion, and synthesis by a chairman model. Credit
for that idea belongs to its author.

This acknowledgement is permanent and unconditional. It does not lapse because
the implementation was rewritten, and it is to be carried forward into every
further application built on this foundation, in any jurisdiction. The insight
came first; everything here followed from it.

The upstream project carries no licence file. Its author released it publicly
stating it was "provided here as is for other people's inspiration". Because
no licence could be relied upon, the implementation here has since been
rewritten: the transport layer, the storage layer, the deliberation prompts
and the request schema were each reimplemented, and what remains in common
with the original is limited to function signatures, dictionary keys, import
statements and framework idiom — matter dictated by the libraries in use
rather than by any authorial choice.

The Apache License 2.0 in the accompanying LICENSE file is granted by
CA Loganathan Anandan over this work.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
ORIGINAL CONTRIBUTIONS OF THIS PROJECT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following are original works of CA Loganathan Anandan, written for this
project and licensed under the Apache License 2.0:

    The adversarial compliance panel — four counsel organised by role in the
    argument, cross-examination in place of ranking, and chairman
    determination returned as a structured professional deliverable.

    Citation verification, including the currency check and the rule that a
    citation is never silently upgraded to verified.

    Enforced identifier anonymisation with a pre-flight leak audit that
    aborts the run rather than transmitting client data.

    Notice intake — local pattern extraction of statutory identifiers, and
    jurisdiction derivation driving binding-versus-persuasive precedent
    weighting.

    Reconciliation ingestion — deterministic local bucketing of input tax
    credit mismatches, designed so that invoice-level data never reaches a
    model.

    The reply pack export, the domain pack interface, and the GST domain
    pack.

